Add converter for legacy Gingko Desktop 2.x .gko archives

Old .gko files are 7z archives containing a PouchDB/leveldb database of
git-like commit/tree/ref objects. On open, detect the 7z signature and
offer conversion: extract with sevenz-rust2, read the leveldb with
rusty-leveldb, walk the head commit's tree, and emit <gingko-card>
markdown (mirroring Coders.treeToMarkdownOutline). The converted
document opens as Untitled, leaving the original file unmodified.

Includes a unit test against a sanitized 2.x archive (tests/historic).

